. Executive summary
The discussion established two immediate priorities: complete forensic transaction analysis of eight high-priority bank accounts and extraction of FedWire transactions across all accounts with available FedWire documentation.
The client has approximately 28 bank accounts in the production, but does not require full forensic analysis of every account. The immediate emphasis is on producing reliable, traceable transaction data from the eight priority accounts while also capturing wire activity across the broader account population.
A critical requirement is to avoid double-counting transactions appearing in multiple sources, such as bank statements, Excel transaction listings, and PDF wire confirmations.
The client prefers incremental delivery of completed account files, rather than waiting for the entire analysis to be completed.
