9. Overall recommendation
Given the deadline pressure, run the priority-account analysis and FedWire extraction as parallel workstreams rather than processing them sequentially.
The first meaningful output should be a fully extracted and reconciled account workbook accompanied by a source-reference index. This provides the legal team with something immediately usable while other accounts are being processed.
Once the account-level and FedWire datasets are sufficiently complete, move to inter-account tracing and cash-focused analytics. Broader pattern analysis and DOJ public-record enrichment should remain secondary unless a particular transaction raises an urgent investigative question.
The definition of success is not merely extracting data into Excel. It is creating a single, financially reconciled, source-supported record of what happened to the funds, suitable for further investigation, legal analysis and deposition preparation.
